gradio-file-endpoint-is-in-or-equal-bypass — repro / gate log
=============================================================
Date: 2026-07-14
Host: real Docker (Docker 29.4.0), official PyPI gradio wheels on python:3.11-slim.

SINK (source-verified from gradio/utils.py at each tag; same is_in_or_equal reached via
the gradio/routes.py `/file=` route):
  V0 gradio 4.10.0 : if str(path_1.relative_to(path_2)).startswith(".."): return False
  V1 gradio 4.11.0 : if ".." in str(path_1.relative_to(path_2)): return False        # CVE-2023-51449 fix
  V2 gradio 5.0.0  : path_1, path_2 = abspath(path_1).resolve(), abspath(path_2).resolve(); path_1.relative_to(path_2)  # CVE-2024-47164 fix
  (abspath() in 4.10/4.11 returns absolute inputs UN-normalized and explicitly "does not
   resolve symlinks"; 5.0.0 adds .resolve() which normalizes ".." AND resolves symlinks.
   5.0.0 also relocated the route under API_PREFIX -> `/gradio_api/file=`, same sink.)

ENV: minimal stock gr.Interface launched on 0.0.0.0:7860 with allowed_paths=["/gradio_tmp"].
