VERDICT: GATE PASSED — genuine incomplete-fix pair.
  The 4.11.0 fix for CVE-2023-51449 hardened is_in_or_equal against a literal ".."
  ANYWHERE in the relative path, closing the subdir+".." escape. But the SAME
  containment guard still trusted abspath(), which never resolved symlinks, so a
  symlink inside the allowed dir escaped it (CVE-2024-47164). 5.0.0 closed it by
  adding .resolve() to the same is_in_or_equal function.

NOTE: A pure literal-".." residual is caught by V1's substring check, so the genuine
V1-surviving residual is the symlink form (closed by V2's .resolve()). See
_heldout/evidence.json.

